The ISO 3166-1 country registry in src/countrycodes/country.py is
derived from the iso-codes project, version 4.16.0:
https://salsa.debian.org/iso-codes-team/iso-codes

Copyright (c) 2001-2008 Alastair McKinstry
Copyright (c) 2004-2016 Christian Perrier
Copyright (c) 2005-2024 Dr. Tobias Quathamer

The bundled Python registry is an adapted subset of the upstream ISO 3166-1
records. It retains alpha-2, alpha-3, numeric, and name fields (including
optional official and common names), renames the alpha code keys to the
library's schema, and omits unrelated upstream fields. It also includes
continent display names derived from the GeoNames data described below.

The registry data is licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License,
version 2.1 or (at your option) any later version. The license text is
included in iso-codes.LGPL-2.1.txt. The countrycodes project code is separately
licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License; see the LICENSE file.

The continent assignments are derived from the Continent field in GeoNames
countryInfo.txt, downloaded 2026-10-28:
https://download.geonames.org/export/dump/countryInfo.txt

The international dial codes are derived from the Phone field in GeoNames
countryInfo.txt, downloaded 2026-10-29. They contain the country calling code,
excluding any area-code portion supplied by GeoNames.

GeoNames data is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International License (CC BY 4.0):
